{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedQuantumDimension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.BraidedQuantumDimension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Braided"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_rightDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_rightDual","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedQuantumDimension.lean#L110-L124","doc":"**The braided quantum dimension is conjugation-symmetric**: `qDim(Xᘁ) = qDim(X)`, in any\nbraided right-rigid category, with no pivotal, spherical or transport hypothesis.\n\nBoth duals of `Xᘁ` — the canonical `Xᘁᘁ` and the swapped `X` — give the same dimension by\n`qDimWith_congr_dual`; against the swapped one it is `qDim(X)` by `qDimWith_swap`.\n\nDistinct from `QOU.BraidKnot.C2QDimTranspose.qDim_conj`, which is the partition-transpose statement\n`d_q(λ) = d_q(λ')` over `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_swap","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedQuantumDimension.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**Against the swapped pairing, the dimension of `Xᘁ` is the dimension of `X`.**\n\n`BraidedCategory.exactPairing_swap` makes `X` a right dual of `Xᘁ`, with coevaluation\n`η_ X Xᘁ ≫ (β_ Xᘁ X).inv` and evaluation `(β_ X Xᘁ).hom ≫ ε_ X Xᘁ`. The `β⁻¹` the coevaluation\ncarries meets the trace's own `β` and cancels, leaving `qDim(X)` exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_congr_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith_congr_dual","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedQuantumDimension.lean#L82-L98","doc":"**The quantum dimension does not depend on the choice of dual.**\n\n`rightDualIso p₁ p₂ : B₁ ≅ B₂` is the comparison map. Mathlib's\n`coevaluation_comp_rightAdjointMate` and `rightAdjointMate_comp_evaluation`, at `f = 𝟙 A` with\nmixed instances, say exactly that it transports `η` and `ε` between the two pairings; braiding\nnaturality then slides it from one side of the crossing to the other, where the two occurrences\ncancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.qDimWith","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/BraidedQuantumDimension.lean#L76-L80","doc":"**The braided quantum dimension** of `A` taken against a *named* right dual `B`: the ribbon\ntrace of the identity, `η ≫ β ≫ ε`. Writing the dual explicitly is what lets `qDimWith_congr_dual`\nsay the choice does not matter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}